<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Larache</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Larache is a port city on the Atlantic coast of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> at the mouth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/loukkos">Loukkos</a> river, near the ruins of ancient Lixus. A Saadi port, it was handed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in 1610, recaptured by the Alaouite sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moulay-ismail">Moulay Ismail</a> in 1689, and was again under Spanish rule as part of the Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> in Morocco from 1911 to 1956.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/larache.jpg" alt="Larache" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ideophagous · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Old_walls_in_Larache_6.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The kingdom split between rival rulers at Fez and Marrakesh, and in 1610 al-Ma’mun handed the port of <b>Larache</b> to Spain in return for support, a concession that discredited the dynasty.</blockquote><a href="/empire/saadi-sultanate">Saadi Sultanate · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>He recovered Tangier, La Mamora and <b>Larache</b> from Europeans.</blockquote><a href="/state/alaouite-sultanate">Alaouite Sultanate</a></li><li><blockquote>Lixus lay on a hill above the Loukkos river near modern <b>Larache</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/lixus">Lixus</a></li><li><blockquote>Spain took <b>Larache</b> in 1610 and La Mamora in 1614 as the Saadi Sultanate fell apart.</blockquote><a href="/state/marabout-state-of-al-ayyashi">Marabout state of al-Ayyashi</a></li></ul></section>
